# Page a long selection menu with the RIGHT arrow, not TAB: inc-7h6s.
#
# The Steam Deck maps a stick to the arrow keys, so a player has Right and Left
# at hand but not Tab. A single-column paged LMenu must therefore page on Right
# (forward) and Left (back), mirroring Tab and Shift-Tab. This script proves the
# forward half on the same menu tools/keys/menu-overflow.keys uses.
#
# WHY THIS CHARACTER. A Wood Elf Druid at seed 7 is offered 88 feats, more than
# the 52 letters a page can show, so the list pages. Natural Aptitude is the
# 61st of the 88 -- it is NOT on the first page. The only way to reach it is to
# turn the page.
#
# WHAT MAKES IT AN ORACLE. This script turns the page with RIGHT, never TAB. On
# a build without the inc-7h6s change RIGHT does the old within-page column move
# and never crosses a page boundary, so "Natural Aptitude" never appears, the
# @until below exhausts, and the run fails instead of reaching @choose. So a
# green run proves RIGHT paged the menu forward. @choose then reads the letter
# the game printed beside the name, so the feat was also selectable, not merely
# visible.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Wood Elf"
@choose "Druid"
a       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
e       # Alignment: [e] Neutral

@expect "Choose a feat"
@until "Natural Aptitud" RIGHT   # RIGHT pages the menu forward, not TAB
@choose "Natural Aptitude"
@expect "Choose a skill"
@choose "Alchemy"                # a skill no druid carries, so the sheet
                                 #   showing it is the feat having worked

@while "Choose a feat" a         # whatever else the class asks for
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y                          # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks
a                                # Personality archetype
@while "Choose a feat" a
a a a a                          # starting spells

@until "Entry Chamber" ESC       # in play
d                                # character sheet
@until "Natural Aptitude" PGDN   # scroll to the Feats block
@dump:sheet-feats
ESC
@quit
